# Yorilife ERP

Custom ERP for Yorilife Sciences. React web app and a framework-free PHP REST API. They talk only over JSON at `/api`. The API must stay usable by a future mobile app (no React knowledge in PHP).

```
frontend/   React 19, Vite 8, React Router 7, Bootstrap 5.3, JS (no TypeScript)
backend/    PHP 8.3, PDO, MySQL 8. PSR-4 App\ under controllers, services, middleware, repositories, database, utils
docs/       ARCHITECTURE.md, DATA_MODEL.md, SPRINT_PLAN.md — read these before changing auth, schema, or business rules
```

## Sprint map

Sprints 1–5 are done. Sprint 4 persists the business modules. Sales Final Value is stored as entered and is never calculated. All signed-in users see all business records. Sales Manager and Sales User are view-only. Only Admin and Super Admin restore catalogue terms and products.

Sprint 5 adds headquarters state, address, pincode, and phone, and fictional Sales Office demo data via `php bin/seed-demo.php` (development database `yorilife_erp` only). The chain reads from the top: 3rd line manager, then 2nd line manager, then 1st line manager, then headquarters, then stockists. A 3rd line manager has no parent. Stockists link only to a headquarters. State is one of the 28 states or 8 union territories in `backend/config/states.php` (`Delhi`, not a longer label).

Do not rebuild those modules. Dashboard, Reports, Announcements, Application Details, a general audit log, settings, and CSV import are still placeholders. Do not invent their formulas, columns, or workflows. Details are in `docs/SPRINT_PLAN.md`.

## Local run

- API: `php -S localhost:8000 -t public public/index.php` from `backend/` (or `composer serve`). PHP is often not on PATH; Laragon: `C:\laragon\bin\php\php-8.3.30-Win32-vs16-x64\php.exe`.
- Web: `npm run dev` in `frontend/` → `http://localhost:5173`. Vite proxies `/api` to `:8000`.
- Databases: `yorilife_erp` (dev) and `yorilife_erp_test` (tests only). Tests refuse any database whose name does not end in `_test` and wipe test users. Never point tests at `yorilife_erp`.
- Migrations: `php bin/migrate.php` (forward-only SQL in `backend/database/migrations/`). No down migrations. First Super Admin: `php bin/create-admin.php` (no default password).

## Do not

- Put secrets, session IDs, password hashes, or CSRF tokens in responses, URLs, logs, or frontend storage.
- Change the official logo file or crop it. Render it only through `BrandLogo.jsx`.
- Add a permissions table or JWT until that decision is explicit. Web auth stays cookie sessions.
